(D) THE FINITE PROBLEM lives on Z/Phi6, CRT-factored over the primes of Phi6, mod antipode Z/2:
    Z/183 = Z/3 x Z/61  (CRT over primes of Phi6)
    prime 2 (the FIRST prime) = the antipode iota: p <-> -p (t<->1-t). The finite covering problem
