    gcd(n,Phi6)=1 (n is a unit mod Phi6 => p(w)=n*w is a BIJECTION Z/Phi6->Z/Phi6).

=> CORRECTED REDUCTION (honest): the SCALE-INVARIANT finite structure is the DIFFERENCE SET.
   - single-far: phase = p(w)∈Z/Phi6 (DIRECTION); magnitude = width O(1/w) -> 0 (impotent, S66).
   - PAIRWISE: corr2(a,a+δ) depends ONLY on the difference δ (scale-invariant: same for a=300..2000),
     via p(δ)=nδ mod Phi6; LARGE & POSITIVE (redundant) iff δ∈(n-1)Z with δ small (S67).
   So multi-far coupling is governed by the DIFFERENCE-SET {w_i-w_j} and its phase-residues in
   Z/Phi6 (translation-invariant) -- and the magnitude on the resonance lattice (n-1)Z is the
   ADDITIVE ENERGY of the far-speed set (HYP-2873/THM-515). Redundancy(+)=helps survival;
   spreading(-)=weak. The FINITE object is the difference-set's phase-histogram on Z/Phi6.
